# Bulk data — NEVER commit. `data/` holds only regenerable artefacts: the ~135 MB ITF
# snapshot (re-fetchable), its Parquet derivatives, cached MPEC HTML, and Find_Orb working
# directories. Ignored wholesale so a new working directory can never be added by accident.
#
# One exception in spirit: `data/snapshots/` is the ITF archive, and history only
# accumulates forward, so it genuinely cannot be regenerated. It is still far too large for
# git and needs its own backup if it is ever to be relied on.
# Anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored `data/` would also swallow `tests/data/`,
# which holds the committed fixtures the whole test suite runs against.
/data/
*.parquet
*.txt.gz

# Generated reports. The committed narrative lives in M0-RESULTS.md / M1-RESULTS.md.
m0-report.json
m1-report.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Secrets (no credentials are needed today; belt-and-suspenders for M3 submission work)
.env
*.token
secrets/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
